=== SURVEY ===
  Web source of truth — web/src/components/ui/Drawer.tsx:
    A portal-rendered, purely-presentational slide-in side panel. Props:
      open, onClose, title?, children, footer?, side ('left'|'right', default 'right'),
      className?.
    Behaviour: role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label={title || 'Panel'}; a fading
      backdrop scrim (bg var(--surface-overlay) + blur) that closes on click
      (aria-hidden); a panel that springs in from the side (x 100%→0 right / -100%→0
      left); a titled header (rendered only when `title`) with an `<h3>` + a close
      `<button aria-label="Close"><X/></button>`; a scrollable flex-1 body (children);
      an optional footer over an overlay surface; a focus trap (focus first focusable,
      Tab/Shift-Tab cycle), Escape-to-close, and focus restore on unmount.
    Literal strings: just the `aria-label={title || 'Panel'}` fallback + close
      `aria-label="Close"`. No data hooks; no loading/empty/error/stale/offline of its
      own (those belong to whatever `children` it hosts). The prompt itself records
      "Data sources: (none — pure presentational component)".
  Existing native code inspected (to match conventions, not duplicated):
    Sources/Components/UI/Overlays.swift — the ATOMIC `tsDrawer` modifier + TSDrawerEdge
      (the P4 component-library bundle's scope, OUT of scope here; NOT modified/redeclared).
    TeslaSync/feature-views/{ToolCard,FSMTimelineChart}.* — the established per-surface
      file layout (Telemetry/Model/Adapter/Views/Previews/strings/Tests), telemetry seam,
      P1/S10 NSLocalizedString table facade, and the ADR-013 freshness envelope.
    Sources/Components/Feedback/{States,Skeletons}.swift — TSSkeleton (used), the
      ContentUnavailableView empty treatment, the QueryError retry treatment (mirrored).

=== REASONING ===
  Chosen approach: a self-contained, model-driven SwiftUI surface `Drawer(model:)` that
    reproduces the web component's composition + behaviour (edge-anchored sliding glass
    panel over a tap-to-dismiss scrim; titled header with close; scrollable body; footer)
    AND hosts a representative data-bound body so EVERY prompt-required state renders
    INSIDE the panel — loading (skeleton rows), empty (ContentUnavailableView), error
    (retry), stale (chip + one auto-refresh), offline (cached body + chip), content
    (label/value rows). Binding flows through a `DrawerSource` seam (P1/S8); the view
    never networks. Dismissal (web `onClose`) is one path shared by the scrim tap, the
    close button, the footer action, and the Escape key (the close button's
    `.cancelAction` shortcut). Presentation moves VoiceOver focus onto the panel (web
    "focus the first focusable") and marks it `.isModal`. Motion honours Reduce Motion.
  Rejected: (a) porting the web Tailwind classes / framer-motion spring literally —
    replaced with platform materials + tokens + a native spring/transition per ADR HIG;
    (b) re-using/!redeclaring the atomic `tsDrawer` modifier (out of scope, and a name
    collision) — the surface composes its own chrome instead; (c) a generic
    `Drawer<Content,Footer>` with no model — it could not satisfy the prompt's mandatory
    loading/empty/error/stale/offline states (the web container delegates those to its
    children), so the surface binds a `DrawerModel` that drives them, the same way the
    FSM/feature-view precedents widen a web content/empty split into the full envelope.

